s:\n\n\\[\nC = W(t_0) \\exp\\left( -\\int_{t_0}^t p(s)\\, ds \\right).\n\\]\n\nSince \\( C \\) and \\( W(t_0) \\) are constants, the exponential factor must be constant for all \\( t \\). That means:\n\n\\[\n\\exp\\left( -\\int_{t_0}^t p(s)\\, ds \\right) = \\text{constant}.\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Conclude about \\( p(t) \\)**  \nThe only way the integral \\(\\int_{t_0}^t p(s)\\, ds\\) is constant for all \\( t \\) is if \\( p(t) = 0 \\) for all \\( t \\).\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{p(t) = 0}\n\\]\n\nThis is the result: if the Wronskian is constant, then \\( p(t) \\) must be identically zero."}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}, {'name': 'openai.chat.completion', 'context': {'trace_id': '0xa3aaeca7a8c5cd715a117f54a146cd09', 'span_id': '0xad3cd01493aa2095', 'trace_state': '[]'}, 'kind': 'SpanKind.CLIENT', 'parent_id': '0x36a5adb404ed7882', 'start_time': '2026-08-25T06:05:37.046667Z', 'end_time': '2026-08-25T06:05:39.320039Z', 'status': {'status_code': 'OK'}, 'attributes': {'gen_ai.request.type': 'chat', 'gen_ai.system': 'OpenAI', 'gen_ai.request.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.request.max_tokens': 4000, 'gen_ai.request.temperature': 0, 'gen_ai.request.top_p': 0.99, 'gen_ai.request.streaming': False, 'gen_ai.prompt.0.role': 'system', 'gen_ai.prompt.0.content': 'You are a helpful assistant.', 'gen_ai.prompt.1.role': 'user', 'gen_ai.prompt.1.content': '\nTask: Evaluate if the current memory is complete and accurate enough to answer the query, or if more tools are needed.\n\nContext:\n- **Query:** Given the second-order linear differential equation \\( \\frac{d^2x}{dt^2} + p(t)\\frac{dx}{dt} + q(t)x = 0 \\), find the function \\( p(t) \\) if the Wronskian of two solutions \\( x_1(t) \\) and \\( x_2(t) \\) is a non-zero constant. Use Abel\'s theorem to determine \\( p(t) \\). When ready, output the f